IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 216: quorum and required vote for stock corporations.
-- Layer 1, from the text alone. Quote lines are copied from de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script.
--
-- Counts are VOTES, not shares (s 212(a): where the certificate gives more or less than 1 vote per share, every reference to
-- a majority or other proportion of stock refers to the votes of that stock); where each share has one vote they are equal.
-- The section applies to a corporation "authorized to issue stock"; s 215(a) says it does not apply to nonstock corporations.
-- The votes of the core's `the vote carries` answer NOTHING when the counts cannot be a vote (a base of 0 or less, or votes
-- in favor below 0 or above the base); that NOTHING is carried up, never turned into FALSE.

§ `s 216 Quorum and required vote for stock corporations`

§§ `s 216 chapeau: the quorum the certificate or bylaws may set, and its floor`

-- Subject to this chapter in respect of the vote required for a specified action, the certificate of incorporation or the
-- bylaws may specify the number of shares and/or the amount of other securities having voting power the holders of which
-- shall be present or represented by proxy at a meeting to constitute a quorum, and the votes necessary for the transaction of
-- any business, but in no event shall a quorum consist of less than 1/3 of the shares entitled to vote at the meeting, except
-- that where a separate vote by a class or series is required a quorum shall consist of no less than 1/3 of the shares of that
-- class or series.
-- The base of a quorum is the votes entitled to vote at the meeting or, for a class or series voting separately, the votes
-- of that class or series. A specification below 1/3 is read as a quorum of 1/3: the section says "in no event ... less than
-- 1/3", not that the specification fails (fork F-Q). With no specification the default in paragraph (1) (or (4) for a
-- separate vote) applies: a majority.
-- src:812 | Subject to this chapter in respect of the vote that shall be required for a specified action, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of any corporation authorized to issue stock may specify the number of shares and/or the amount of other securities having voting power the holders of which shall be present or represented by proxy at any meeting in order to constitute a quorum for, and the votes that shall be necessary for, the transaction of any business, but in no event shall a quorum consist of less than 1/3 of the shares entitled to vote at the meeting, except that, where a separate vote by a class or series or classes or series is required, a quorum shall consist of no less than 1/3 of the shares of such class or series or classes or series. …
-- The specified quorum, floored at 1/3 of the votes entitled, as a proportion of those votes.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 216 (src:812)
GIVEN specified IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes entitled to vote at the meeting, or of the class or series voting separately` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
